# CUDA-graph capture for the DFlash2 decode/verify hot path (DRAFT, NOT APPLIED)
#
# Base: 1359c43 (2026-08-29). Region analysis, vetoed regions, savings
# arithmetic, integration checklist and the fallback contract are in the
# accompanying review message; this file is only the diff. Hunk headers were
# hand-computed against the files as of the base commit; expect `git apply
# --recount` to normalize counts.
#
# Determinism argument (the law, applied to graphs): a graph captured from a
# single stream records the exact kernel nodes (function, grid, block, shared
# memory, parameter bytes) in the recorded stream order and replays them as
# that same chain - nothing is fused, reordered, or re-associated. Every
# kernel sees bit-identical inputs because the only per-round scalars
# (anchor_position / ctx_len / RoPE pos0) move from by-value kernel arguments
# to a pinned host scalar whose H2D copy is the first node of the graph:
# replays re-read the pinned integer, so the kernels compute with the very
# integers they used to receive by value. The replay stream is
# legacy-synchronizing (cudaStreamCreate), preserving today's fully
# serialized execution order. Acceptance test = the parity gate: greedy IDs,
# digit-identical top-10 logits, 30/40/100/240-token sequence checks.
#
# Regions captured:
#   R1 "df-forward" : 5-layer drafter block forward          144 kernels + 1 D2D memcpy
#   R2 "df-head"    : 7x lm_head FP8 GEMV on draft hiddens    14 kernels
#   R3 "verify-tail": avg-streams + final RMS + lm_head rows  1 + 3*count kernels
#                     (keyed by count; padding to 8 was analyzed and rejected:
#                      bit-safe but multiplies lm_head traffic by 8/count)
# Regions deliberately NOT captured (host data-dependent control flow, see
# message): sparse_moe / moe_multi / mtp_moe expert chains, router downloads,
# ExpertStager upload loops, MLA latent path (grid varies with position),
# KDA chains (need position indirection; phase 2).
#
# Env surface: INSIGNIA_GLM53_GRAPHS=0 hard-disables; any DF_DUMP / DF_LTRACE
# / DF_ITRACE / CHECK_LINEAR session silently keeps the uncaptured path.

